      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As a user who has dabbled in various tracking methods including Amethyst (Microsoft Kinect-based tracking), PSMSX (Playstation Move Service Ex-based tracking), and now getting into SlimeVR IMU-based tracking, i can 100% agree being able to save calibrations between sessions is crucial for instant hop-in-and-go playability.\n\nNumerous times i've been off-put from hopping into VRC due to the headache that is having to calibrate EVERY SINGLE TIME i go to get in and run buck wild.\n\nAmethyst and SlimeVR are basically guaranteed setups on every boot so long as Stage Tracking is enabled in Steam Link, ALVR, or Virtual Desktop for SLAM-tracked HMDs, as both use the HMD as the reference point to base tracking lower than the head off of.\n\nPSMSX is more similar to Lighthouse-based solutions in that it uses cameras to blob-track the trackers with cameras similar to the lasers of the Lighthouse ecosystem, so i'd understand those are more prone to move somewhat between new sessions, barring crashes of course.\n\nBut in the instance of the infamous crashes VRC is prone to for whichever reason, being able to save my calibration values would be an absolute godsend of an update. Heck, if people are using straps that nearly guarantee exact mounting positions every time, even Lighthouse-based solutions could greatly benefit from such an update.\n\nTL;DR of this wall of text, frickin do it we'd like probably go legitimately nutter for this kind of an update! :)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
